wolf3d-portable @PROJECT_VERSION@ - Linux direct-console host
=========================================================

This package runs directly on a Linux virtual console. It does not require
X11, Wayland, SDL, or a desktop environment. Video uses DRM/KMS dumb buffers,
input uses evdev, and audio uses ALSA.

Copy the original game data files beside the executable, or point to them:

  ./wolf3d --data /path/to/WL1

Run it from an active virtual console. The user needs permission to access the
DRM card, evdev input devices, and ALSA playback device; root normally has all
three. Typical non-root installations grant this through the distribution's
video, input, and audio groups or through seat/session device ACLs.

Host-specific options:

  --drm-device /dev/dri/card0
  --input-device /dev/input/event3    (repeatable)
  --alsa-device default
  --no-audio
  --linux-console-help

Game audio options are --opl nuked|dbopl|silent and --sample-rate HZ. Only
drivers recorded in WOLF3D-LIB.txt are available.

Without explicit device options, the host selects the first connected DRM
display, opens usable evdev devices, and uses the ALSA "default" PCM. Missing
or unavailable audio produces a warning and the game continues silently.

The host preserves the engine's 320x200 indexed framebuffer and displays it
at the original monitor-intended 4:3 aspect ratio with letterboxing as needed.

libwolf3d.so is the generic engine library. When present, libNuked-OPL3.so is
kept separate and replaceable under the LGPL-2.1 license. System libdrm, ALSA,
libc, and their dependencies must be supplied by the target Linux installation.

See LICENSE.txt for wolf3d-portable's license, LICENSES/ for the explicit
wolf3d-lib and applicable component license texts, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt for
component provenance.
